1
00:00:01,290 --> 00:00:04,130
Hi there! It's great to have you back.

2
00:00:04,130 --> 00:00:08,280
So far, we've talked about tracking and
measuring project progress.

3
00:00:08,280 --> 00:00:11,756
We've also discussed how to manage
quality through different techniques and

4
00:00:11,756 --> 00:00:14,190
the benefits of continuous improvement.

5
00:00:14,190 --> 00:00:19,110
Now, I'm going to tell you all about
data and data-informed decision making.

6
00:00:19,110 --> 00:00:21,350
You'll learn how data impacts decisions,

7
00:00:21,350 --> 00:00:24,440
some of which occur
during a project journey.

8
00:00:24,440 --> 00:00:28,538
You'll get answers to questions like:
How do I use data in my project?

9
00:00:28,538 --> 00:00:30,879
Which types of data should I search for?

10
00:00:30,879 --> 00:00:34,040
And how do I determine what
stakeholders need to know?

11
00:00:35,360 --> 00:00:39,813
Now, more than ever, we have access to
data at our fingertips on our computers,

12
00:00:39,813 --> 00:00:41,590
tablets, and phones.

13
00:00:41,590 --> 00:00:45,348
We use data every day to view
the stats of our favorite athletes,

14
00:00:45,348 --> 00:00:50,030
examine our screen time on social media,
and monitor our health.

15
00:00:50,030 --> 00:00:52,486
Data is a part of our daily lives.

16
00:00:52,486 --> 00:00:56,310
Take, for example, online job search sites.

17
00:00:56,310 --> 00:01:00,716
These companies collect basic data you
enter—like your previous experience,

18
00:01:00,716 --> 00:01:04,319
location, maybe any degrees or
certificates you might hold—and

19
00:01:04,319 --> 00:01:08,070
use that information to determine
potential job matches for you.

20
00:01:09,220 --> 00:01:13,072
Jobs that don't fit the criteria of what
you entered aren't likely to appear in

21
00:01:13,072 --> 00:01:14,880
your suggestions.

22
00:01:14,880 --> 00:01:19,900
This is just one way data is used to
inform and influence our decisions.

23
00:01:19,900 --> 00:01:24,874
In this module, we'll discuss project data
and how it informs decision-making and

24
00:01:24,874 --> 00:01:28,490
helps to prevent both major and
minor issues.

25
00:01:28,490 --> 00:01:34,200
We'll also discuss how project-related
data can be used to reach success metrics.

26
00:01:34,200 --> 00:01:38,608
We'll go over common project data, such
as tasks and issues, and discuss how

27
00:01:38,608 --> 00:01:43,970
analyzing this data and other metrics
impacts project productivity and quality.

28
00:01:43,970 --> 00:01:47,650
Finally, we'll demonstrate how
data isn't just about numbers.

29
00:01:47,650 --> 00:01:50,770
You can also tell a unique
story using the power of data.

30
00:01:51,920 --> 00:01:55,710
Storytelling offers a memorable way
to communicate important aspects of

31
00:01:55,710 --> 00:01:57,390
your project.

32
00:01:57,390 --> 00:01:59,928
Pairing storytelling
with data can convince

33
00:01:59,928 --> 00:02:04,690
stakeholders of ways to resolve problems
and ensure a successful outcome.

34
00:02:04,690 --> 00:02:06,520
So data certainly has its benefits.

35
00:02:07,820 --> 00:02:09,840
There's a lot to learn about data,

36
00:02:09,840 --> 00:02:13,713
and we'll lay out some of the basics so
you can confidently tackle your projects.

37
00:02:13,713 --> 00:02:15,330
Ready to get started?

38
00:02:15,330 --> 00:02:16,530
Let's get to it in the next video.
